{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-puzzle-solving", "file": "references/periodic-stripe-sequence.md", "content": "# Periodic stripe grids: global-sequence hypothesis

When demos are made of uniform-color rows or columns, reason over the 1D stripe sequence as well as individual cells. Compare the input stripe sequence with the full output sequence, including repeated periods and boundary phase. A transformation may generate a periodic color sequence from a compact set of stripe exemplars rather than preserve or locally extend the visible rows. Extract the exact sequence from every demo, test candidate periods and phase, and verify every output stripe before transferring to the test. Do not extrapolate from a single visually suggestive sample; request another demo if the rule connecting input stripe order to output period remains ambiguous.
